  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\), \\(AB=AC\\), and \\(D\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\). Find the measure of \\(\\angle ADB\\) in degrees.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "90",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "By SSS, \\(\\triangle ABD\\cong\\triangle ACD\\), so \\(\\angle ADB=\\angle ADC\\). Also, \\(\\angle ADB+\\angle ADC=180^\\circ\\), hence \\(\\angle ADB=90^\\circ\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the isosceles median property\n\nSince \\(AB=AC\\), the triangle is isosceles with base \\(BC\\). Because \\(D\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\), \\(AD\\) is the median to the base. In an isosceles triangle, this median is also an altitude, so \\(AD\\perp BC\\). Therefore \\(\\angle ADB=90^\\circ\\).",
